On Mon, Jun 23, 2014 at 2:46 AM, Gleki Arxokuna <gleki.is.my.name@gmail.com>
wrote:

> since a new vlatai based on camxes PEG is implemented in JVS, the word
> {geimast} isno longer a valid lojban word and disappeared from the db.
>
> Thus I'd like to know can we change the PEG morphology so that {geimast}
> is valid again?
>

The morphology in
http://www.lojban.org/tiki/BPFK+Section%3A+PEG+Morphology+Algorithm has
allowed free form cmevla with non-Lojbanic syllables since 2007, so the
parser must be using an older version.

mu'o mi'e xorxes

